        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of காயம் (kāyam), \"wound\", is uncertain. DEDR does not give this sense, but it lists kāyam, \"scar\", beside kāy, \"to form a callus, as from a wound\" (DEDR 1460), and the two may be one word. Another possible source is Prakrit ghāya, \"wound\" (CDIAL 4460)."
            }
          ]
        },
